<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">10 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 10 May, from 1503 to 1940.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1503 CE <span class="tih-ago">523 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Columbus sights the Cayman Islands</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On his fourth voyage, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a> sighted two small islands teeming with turtles, which he named Las Tortugas. They later became known as the Cayman Islands.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1773 CE <span class="tih-ago">253 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Parliament passes the Tea Act</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Act let the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> ship <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tea">tea</a> directly to America, undercutting smugglers while keeping the Townshend duty. Colonists saw it as a ploy to make them accept taxation, leading to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston-tea-party">Boston Tea Party</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1775 CE <span class="tih-ago">251 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Second Continental Congress meets in Philadelphia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Delegates from the colonies gathered weeks after Lexington and Concord. The Congress created the Continental Army, appointed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington">George Washington</a> to command it and declared independence in 1776.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1863 CE <span class="tih-ago">163 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Stonewall Jackson dies of pneumonia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Eight days after being wounded by his own men at Chancellorsville, General Thomas 'Stonewall' Jackson died. Lee said he had lost his right arm.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1865 CE <span class="tih-ago">161 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Union cavalry capture Jefferson Davis in Georgia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The fleeing Confederate president was seized near Irwinville, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>. He was held for two years at Fort Monroe but never brought to trial.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1869 CE <span class="tih-ago">157 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Golden spike completes the first transcontinental railroad</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Central Pacific and Union Pacific lines met at Promontory Summit, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/utah">Utah</a>. Coast-to-coast travel fell from months to about a week, at great cost to Native American lands.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1940 CE <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Churchill becomes Prime Minister as Germany attacks in the West</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">As German forces invaded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a> and Luxembourg, Neville Chamberlain resigned and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winston-churchill">Winston Churchill</a> formed a coalition government to lead <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>'s war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a></div></div></li></ol>
